This term was first coined in 1990s and since then it is used as a global management practice.
1.	Connecting to campus: Companies these days are launching various programs to connect to campuses[.] It is a kind of background integration so as to attract the talent[.] By this way, companies also[ enhance] the pool for right talent[.
]2.	Including motivational factors in EVP[:] Inclusion[ of] motivational[ factors] other than hygiene factors[ is very] important[ to] stand[ apart] from competitors[. Motiv]ational factors like global exposure,[ ment]orship and sponsorships programs etc.[ can be] added to[ make] EV[P more] lucrative[.
]3.	Collaborating with marketing team: Companies HRs can collaborate with marketing teams so as to advertise their EVP and[ create a] pool of right talent to tap upon. To create the right supply, companies need to create the right demand[ and] for that companies sometimes need to reframe their perception in the market.
4.	Increasing visibility of successful employees[:] By making successful[ employees] of their[ company] visible, companies[ can] leverage upon their career progression[ plans] for[ employees.] Successful[ employees can act as] model for other employees as well[ as] perspective employees. Future employees[ would] see[ getting] into the[ company as a] successful step for corporate ladder[.
