[For] example, in JEE[ or G]ATE, for multiple choice questions, we have one answer and four choices to choose from. It is not uncommon that sometimes that all the four choices are wrong. The corrective measure taken[ by] the administrator is one of the following: (a) that all students[ who] have attempted the[ question are] given full marks or (b) all students irrespective of whether they have attempted the[ question] are given full marks (c)[ no] one[ is] given marks and the question is not evaluated.
